title: AEKE Reformation
subtitle: Our party's character has been changing...
view-if: year == 1931 and month == 12
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= AEKE Reformation

The power dynamics within and without our party have changed significantly since its founding. In addition to our decisive new course of sction, many members are asking for a change in our image as well. 

Our party's name, [+ de_name +], holds particular gravity in regard to our ideological self-assignment and image to the public. And indeed, many wish to see it change to something that better reflects our current values.

There is precedent to this opinion; <span style="color:lightcoral">AEKE</span> is itself a renaming of Papanastasiou's original party, the <span style="color:#0f8dd6">Democratic Union</span>.

- @nolol: It better fits the demagogues to change their ways in a whim. Our party's name is one.
- @farmers: They are right, for we have become the party of a <span style="color:#057a24">single class</span>.
- @liberal: Perhaps we must revert to our original name, that which is connected with the declaration of the Republic.
- @socialist: Our party's name must reflect our radical platform.

@nolol

We have refused to change our party name.

@farmers
on-arrival: de_name = "EAK"

Our agrarianist members rejoice. We are now the <span style="color:#057a24">United Farmers' Party</span> (EAK).

@liberal
on-arrival: de_name = "DE"

Our progressive liberal elements secure that the Democratic Union reinstates its old image as the party of the Republic.

@socialist
on-arrival: de_name = "SDEK"

It appears that Greece's reformist socialist movement has fully matured, as the <span style="color:#cc0a0a">Social Democratic Workers' Party</span> (SDEK) is born.